[Inflections]
Word: !de, !del, !para, !con, !en

# First and second column are for weak adjectives (which I think is the only thing needed? Considering the context which is item prefixes).
# Most German adjectives are uninflectable, safe for those.
# The rest is all for common noun endings for certain genders.

MascSg: -e,  -X,   -er,      -aXen, -aXXen
FemSg:  -e,  -X,   -erin,    X,     X
NeutSg: -e,  -X,   X,        X,     X
MascPl: -en, -Xen, -ers,     -äXen, -äXXen
FemPl:  -en, -Xen, -erinnen, X,     X
NeutPl: -en, -Xen, X,        X,     X

# IMPORTANT: Above table is currently incomplete!

# Help, I don't speak this language! If you do, what are some common words that
# would fall into the above table, but actually be incorrect?
# If you know of any that would show up in Terraria, check out the other .lplus
# files to learn how to use <Exceptions> and also [Items]!
# - ̈q

[Prefixes]

# This is a common change for all vanilla languages;
# 'Light' the adjective was unanimously translated as either the noun, or a transliteration, in other languages.

<Light:(Leicht)>